Media uploaded through the CMS lands here.

This folder is committed empty so it exists in a fresh clone: tina/config.ts
points mediaRoot at it, and Tina cannot write into a directory that is not
there. Git does not track empty directories, hence this file.

Why uploads live here and not in /images directly: the rest of public/images is
a curated, hand-optimised set with a documented size and format budget
(scripts/optimise-media.mjs). Pointing the media browser at the whole tree
would let an editor overwrite a hand-prepared architectural drawing, and would
show them 54 unreferenced orphan files. Keeping uploads in their own folder
means the curated trees stay developer-managed.

Note for whoever maintains this: scripts/optimise-media.mjs is macOS-only (it
shells out to Clop and sips) and is run by hand, so files uploaded through the
CMS bypass the size budget entirely. Porting it to sharp and running it over
this folder in CI is the fix.
